			"notes": "# 🎉 Furnitures O' Plenty 1.2.0\n\n## 🚀 Multi-Loader Support Update\n\nThis release marks the largest internal refactor in Furnitures O' Plenty's history!\n\nFOP has been migrated to Architectury, allowing the mod to officially support both **Forge** and **Fabric** while maintaining world compatibility.\n\n## ✨ New Features\n\n- 🎉 Added **Fabric** support!\n- 🏗️ Migrated the project to **Architectury** for multi-loader development.\n\n## 🔧 Internal Changes\n\n- ♻️ Completely redesigned the codebase.\n- 📁 Introduced separate **Common**, **Forge**, and **Fabric** source modules.\n- 🧩 Migrated block registration to Architectury's registry system.\n- ⚙️ Improved maintainability and future development workflow.\n\n## 📦 Dependencies\n\n**NEW REQUIRED DEPENDENCY**\n\n- Architectury API\n\nPlease install the appropriate version of Architectury API for your loader.\n\n## ✅ Compatibility\n\n- Minecraft 1.20.1\n- Forge\n- Fabric\n\n## 💾 World Compatibility\n\n- Existing worlds remain compatible.\n- No registry IDs have been changed.\n\n## 📝 Developer Note\n\nAlthough this update contains relatively few gameplay changes, it represents the largest architectural upgrade FOP has ever received. The new multi-loader architecture will make future updates, features, and releases significantly easier to develop and maintain.\n\nThank you for supporting Furnitures O' Plenty! ❤️"
		},
